--
N5008 [dcl.fct.def.default]/5: a special member function may be declared
in the class and explicitly defaulted on its first declaration outside
it (`template <class C> buf<C>::buf(const buf &) = default;'); it is then
user-provided but behaves as the implicit one.  The front end reports
"unexpected statement: default" and drops the copy constructor and the
copy assignment; the leftover `default' statement then reaches symbolic
execution, which aborts ("symex_other.cpp: Unreachable") -- the same
abort as a leftover member_initializer (round 163e): an unconverted
statement is not rejected before symex.  libstdc++'s basic_streambuf defines its copy
constructor and copy assignment this way (streambuf:835/840, the
constructor declared at streambuf:812), dropped in
cpp11_ofstream_from_string and the goto-programs TUs; test_libstdcxx.desc
is that program and forbids only the streambuf:812 drop.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept both programs.  Pre-existing (fails on bin52).
